  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">BEL: Development of home-based palliative care for young adults in the regions (BCH)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will improve the quality of palliative home care provided to young adults with palliative status. And, as a result, it&#x2019;ll improve their quality of life by increasing the level of competence of helping professionals in state social protection institutions (territorial centers for social services) and clinics as well as guardians (including parents) of young adults with palliative status in Mogilev and the Mogilev region.
As part of the project, specialists from the Charitable Children&apos;s Hospice (??H) will conduct approximately 10 training sessions at regional social service centres (RSSC) for social workers, carers, medical staff, other specialists in this field and for guardians/parents of young adults. The topics of the training sessions will include general information about palliative care, home care aspects, technical aids for social rehabilitation, communication, psychological and spiritual aspects of palliative care.</narrative>
  </description>
